## Field-level restriction (the rules to remember)

These mirror the app's client-side capability gates in `src/lib/domain.ts` (`ALLOW`) — if you change a
default there, update this table (and the live Directus permissions) to match, or the UI hides a field
that the raw API still returns.

| Field | Owner | Admin | Warehouse | Production | Finance | Courier | App capability |
|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|---|
| `order_lines.price` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | `seePrices` |
| `orders.customer_contact` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |
| `orders.customer_email` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |
| `orders.customer_address` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |
| `orders.sales` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |
| `orders.sales_rep` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |
| `orders.sales_phone_number` | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | `seeCustomerContact` |

In Directus admin: **Settings → Roles & Permissions → [role] → [collection] → Custom → Field
Permissions** → uncheck the restricted fields for that role. Two collections to touch:
- `order_lines` → uncheck `price` for Warehouse, Production, Courier.
- `orders` → uncheck `customer_contact`, `customer_email`, `customer_address`, `sales`, `sales_rep`,
  `sales_phone_number` for Warehouse, Production.

